cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this result or verification package, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "An Exact Counterexample to Complete-Graph Gate-Count Extremality in Graph-Sampled Random Quantum Circuits"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fletcher
    given-names: Austen M.
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-08-17
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Exact rational verification that, for q=t=2 and epsilon=5/6, the
  graph-sampled architecture on the six-vertex octahedron K_{2,2,2} reaches
  multiplicative-error approximate 2-design status after 9 gates, while K_6
  requires 10 gates. The octahedron has smaller exact multiplicative error
  than K_6 at gate counts 6 through 15, with the ordering reversing at 16.
  A separate checker reconstructs the permutation-state Gram matrix and Haar
  projectors directly and exhaustively evaluates Equation 59. This gives a
  finite counterexample to Conjecture 3 of arXiv:2510.23726v2 as literally
  stated. Additional exact finite witnesses are recorded at n=7 and n=8, with
  no general family theorem claimed.
keywords:
  - random quantum circuits
  - unitary designs
  - graph-sampled circuits
  - multiplicative error
  - exact verification
repository-code: "https://github.com/afletc-a11y/graph-sampled-quantum-circuit-counterexample"
